Ported from this repo's Go code (behavior reimplemented, not
honk code):
- Route table: internal/gateway/routes.go LookupRoute,
  internal/conn/gateway.go:316 (method → http/path/service,
  from internal/proto/routes.json, 258 entries at the M3 base).
- HTTP client invariants: internal/telegram/bot.go BoundClient
  + noFollowRedirect (no proxy env, no redirect following).
- Retry policy: internal/conn/shared.go retryCall +
  internal/conn/gateway.go constants (30s budget, 250ms
  doubling to 4s cap, safe set of 9 POST reads + GET).
- TLS/REALITY config: tls.utls.fingerprint, tls.reality.*
  (internal/outbound/tls.go GatewayTLSOptions default chrome;
  honk boring Chrome-mode + REALITY path, no protocol
  reimplementation).
- Error mapping + exit codes: internal/commands/commands.go
  classifyError (auth 2, gateway 3, timeout 4, cancel 130,
  validation 2, else 1); the phaseExitCode table
  (profilecmd.go:901-929) is NOT used here.

What is NOT in this artifact (M3 scope):
- No network CLI commands wired (M4); castctl-rs still builds
  the offline CLI surface only.
- No bot/keeper/webui.
- No WireGuard: honk has no WireGuard outbound, and M3 does
  not implement it. Userspace WireGuard (boringtun) is M3d,
  a separate PR after M3 (see the M3 plan's D-M3/M3d split).
- "No unsafe" covers castctl glue code only (plan D-M3-7):
  the dependency tree (honk/boring/quinn, including C
  BoringSSL code) contains unsafe code and C builds. Do not
  claim the Rust binary is unsafe-free.

